This strategy applies to companies transitioning from a linear sell-and-forget model to one where products are designed to return. It is particularly relevant for B2B contexts where products are leased or offered as a service (e.g. heavy machinery, medical equipment, office furniture). The designer should work closely with business strategists to ensure the product architecture supports the chosen business model — for instance, if leasing is planned, the product must be robust enough to endure multiple users while remaining economically viable to remanufacture.